WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.392 --> 00:00:01.393
I want the truth

00:00:01.393 --> 00:00:02.728
who this guy really is.

00:00:07.713 --> 00:00:09.548
We have tried everything.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.168
You were the only one who gave us hope.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:13.748
I will try my best.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.793
I’ve been trying to get an angle on this

00:00:17.793 --> 00:00:18.836
medical piece.

00:00:18.836 --> 00:00:19.837
Paolo Macchiarini

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.835
who’s developing artificial organs.

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.330
Medical miracles.

00:00:23.497 --> 00:00:25.416
The work I do, this could change the world.

00:00:26.073 --> 00:00:28.284
I take a 3D-printed trachea

00:00:28.441 --> 00:00:30.735
and transform it into a living organ.

00:00:30.735 --> 00:00:32.236
This is groundbreaking work.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.757
The implications are historic.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.017
Perhaps...

00:00:35.394 --> 00:00:37.021
he’ll even bring the Nobel home.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.024
I’m producing a special about you.

00:00:42.015 --> 00:00:43.308
Your patients,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.428
they really trust you.

00:00:47.636 --> 00:00:48.762
Do you trust me?

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.445
Where is he?

00:00:56.195 --> 00:00:57.404
Just sicker than any of us expected.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:58.376
He wasn’t!

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.044
Why are you not holding him accountable?

00:01:01.618 --> 00:01:04.454
The issues are completely unrelated

00:01:04.454 --> 00:01:05.538
to my procedure.

00:01:06.112 --> 00:01:08.114
You’ve always had great instincts.

00:01:08.971 --> 00:01:10.556
Maybe you should trust them.

00:01:11.661 --> 00:01:14.498
I need you to look into someone for me.

00:01:16.059 --> 00:01:17.393
He’s experimenting on people.

00:01:19.396 --> 00:01:20.522
I want to see it with my own eyes.

00:01:23.264 --> 00:01:24.557
My team and I have to deal with

00:01:24.714 --> 00:01:25.841
very extreme cases.

00:01:26.715 --> 00:01:27.758
Just the ones extreme enough that

00:01:27.758 --> 00:01:29.301
nobody will notice when you kill them.

00:01:31.889 --> 00:01:33.599
History is built on lines

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:34.975
that we must be willing to cross.

00:01:37.956 --> 00:01:39.248
What’d you do, Paolo?

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:40.375
What did you do to them?

00:01:41.095 --> 00:01:43.264
We have to figure out a way to stop this guy.

00:01:45.309 --> 00:01:46.352
She’s sitting there with a

00:01:46.352 --> 00:01:48.104
bloody time bomb in her throat.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:50.500
Clear!

00:01:55.662 --> 00:01:57.122
Welcome back.

